  "cooperative_design": [
    "SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers record first signal only; no async exception and no SIG_IGN transition.",
    "Popen returns and owner assignment completes before synchronous shutdown check.",
    "Normal cleanup never checks or raises for shutdown; first-signal mapping is resolved after owned cleanup.",
    "Public supervisor creates one worker session, retains direct leader with waitid WNOWAIT, TERM/KILLs that group before wait. ECHILD permanently disarms group signals.",
    "Debug runner explicitly exports A01_KERNEL_WORKER=1 to bypass added session. This is lifecycle routing, not security authorization or PID==PGID inference.",
    "Inherited GDB listener descriptors are validated >=64 and preserved using pass_fds. Existing shell target/manifest inode/flock logic retained."
  ],
  "seam_evidence": [
    "Real SIGINT then SIGTERM before Popen returns: owner published, first SIGINT retained, worker reaped, mapped130.",
    "Real SIGINT then SIGTERM at first group signal during normal cleanup: both TERM/KILL group signals complete before reap, first SIGINT retained, mapped130.",
    "Real full-wrapper SIGINT/SIGTERM plus repeat shutdown: all pidfds exited, TCP leases released, stable lock released, owned fixture manifest absent.",
    "Normal worker success also kills lingering TERM-ignoring descendant; reaped/external-reap entries never signal numeric group again."
  ],
